From a14da22a866a91649602174349d288c1b932776f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Paul Lamb <paul@paulscode.com>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 13:36:14 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] fetch_blocks: request MSG_WITNESS_BLOCK, not MSG_BLOCK
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A peer served MSG_BLOCK returns the witness-stripped serialization. The proxy
then re-encoded that and handed it back as the answer to getblock, so every
block it fetched from a peer was missing the segwit marker/flag and every
witness stack — silently, because neither validation catches it: the merkle
root commits to txids (unchanged by stripping) and check_witness_commitment()
short-circuits to true once no transaction carries a witness.

Verified on regtest against an archival peer: before, a fetched block was 216
bytes against the archival node's 252; after, byte-identical.

Consumers see a block whose transactions have correct txids but the wrong
serialization, which breaks anything returning raw transactions to a wallet.
electrs already asks its own p2p peer for WitnessBlock, so a pruning-aware
electrs routing some heights through the proxy would otherwise get a different
serialization above and below the prune height.
---
 src/fetch_blocks.rs | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/fetch_blocks.rs b/src/fetch_blocks.rs
index 8e1bf61..d28154f 100644
--- a/src/fetch_blocks.rs
+++ b/src/fetch_blocks.rs
@@ -289,7 +289,14 @@ async fn fetch_block_from_peer<'a>(
         conn = tokio::task::spawn_blocking(move || {
             RawNetworkMessage {
                 magic,
-                payload: NetworkMessage::GetData(vec![Inventory::Block(hash)]),
+                // WitnessBlock, not Block: MSG_BLOCK makes a segwit-aware peer
+                // serve the *stripped* serialization, so the block that comes
+                // back is missing the marker/flag and every witness stack. It
+                // still passes both checks below — the merkle root commits to
+                // txids, which stripping does not change, and
+                // check_witness_commitment() returns true vacuously once no
+                // transaction carries a witness — so the loss is silent.
+                payload: NetworkMessage::GetData(vec![Inventory::WitnessBlock(hash)]),
             }
             .consensus_encode(&mut *conn)
             .map_err(Error::from)
